{"items":[{"gapId":"n0000044","nodes":[{"text":"The method scales as O(d^3) in both FLOP complexity and parameter count as the number d of residual streams increases.","densityScore":0.92}]},{"gapId":"n0000066","nodes":[{"text":"The matrix M satisfies M^T J_d = M J_d = J_d.","densityScore":0.95}]},{"gapId":"n0000073","nodes":[{"text":"mHC-lite defines learned connections as a convex combination of d! permutation matrices, where d is the number of residual streams.","densityScore":0.94},{"text":"mHC-lite has O(dC · d!) cost and is not tenable when scaling beyond d > 8.","densityScore":0.94}]},{"gapId":"n0000076","nodes":[{"text":"KromHC uses tensor products to train residual connections on a smaller set of exactly double-stochastic matrices, sacrificing expressivity and complete coverage of B_d.","densityScore":0.94},{"text":"KromHC costs O(d^2 C).","densityScore":0.91}]},{"gapId":"n0000091","nodes":[{"text":"The layer update is x_(l+1) = H_l^res x_l + (H_l^post)^T F(H_l^pre x_l, W_l).","densityScore":0.97}]},{"gapId":"n0000145","nodes":[{"text":"AGM^fwd(H_(l→L)^res) = max_i Σ_j |(H_(l→L)^res)_ij|.","densityScore":0.97},{"text":"AGM^bwd(H_(l→L)^res) = max_j Σ_i |(H_(l→L)^res)_ij|.","densityScore":0.97}]},{"gapId":"n0000157","nodes":[{"text":"The set contains complex eigenvalues λ for which H^res v = λv with v ≠ 0 and H^res = P_M(⋯).","densityScore":0.94}]},{"gapId":"n0000162","nodes":[{"text":"The set is {e^(i2πj/d′) | j ∈ [1,d′], d′ ≤ d}.","densityScore":0.96}]}]}
